rgence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n81:     \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n82:   }\n83: }\n\n(End of file - total 83 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 10,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 3,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": true,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json","text":"{\n  \"topic\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 10,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 3,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": true,\n  \"specFolder\": \"\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"\",\n  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"native\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"\",\n    \"parentSessionId\": null,\n    \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n    \"allowedModes\": [\n      \"new\",\n      \"resume\",\n      \"restart\"\n    ],\n    \"deferredModes\": [\n      \"fork\",\n      \"completed-continue\"\n    ],\n    \"generation\": 1,\n    \"continuedFromRun\": null\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"registryFile\": \"research/findings-registry.json\",\n    \"dashboardFile\": \"research/deep-research-dashboard.md\",\n    \"strategyFile\": \"research/deep-research-strategy.md\",\n    \"machineOwnedSections\": [\n      \"key-questions\",\n      \"answered-questions\",\n      \"what-worked\",\n      \"what-failed\",\n      \"exhausted-approaches\",\n      \"ruled-out-directions\",\n      \"divergence-frontier\",\n      \"next-focus\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"capabilityMatrixPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json\",\n  \"capabilityMatrixDocPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md\",\n  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n  \"pauseSentinelPath\": \"research/.deep-research-pause\",\n  \"archiveRoot\": \"research_archive\",\n  \"migrationWindowDays\": 28,\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"research/research.md\": \"mutable\"\n  },\n  \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n    \"description\": \"Fields managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). See optimizer-manifest.json for the canonical tunable/locked field registry.\",\n    \"manifestPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n    \"tunableFields\": [\"convergenceThreshold\", \"stuckThreshold\", \"maxIterations\"],\n    \"lockedFields\": [\"lineage\", \"reducer\", \"fileProtection\", \"sessionId\", \"status\", \"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\", \"antiConvergence.stopPolicy\"],\n    \"promotionMode\": \"advisory-only\"\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":83,"totalLines":83,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json","time":{"start":1786568891013,"end":1786568891017}},"id":"prt_ff7cdd8da001XgZTumWxiYt7yl","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7cdc000001pvCw5GzMAnw4Uc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786568891644,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_rLnFdlQVRVe6ggSjiUSK9547","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from memory_context() results, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]\n\n(End of file - total 188 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep research strategy\"\n  - \"research strategy template\"\n  - \"research session tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n  - \"research stop conditions\"\n  - \"ruled out research directions\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.14.0.19\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy Template\ndescription: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep research strategy\"\n  - \"research strategy template\"\n  - \"research session tracking\"\n  - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n  - \"research stop conditions\"\n  - \"ruled out research directions\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.14.0.19\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n\nRuntime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nServes as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n- **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n- **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\nUse `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n\n- `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n- `text`: question text to promote\n- `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n- `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n- `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n- `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n\nThe reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n\nQuestion ownership is explicit:\n\n- Inbox rows are immutable input.\n- The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n- Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n\nWhen an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n[Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n\n- [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n- [ ] [Question 2]\n- [ ] [Question 3]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n[What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n[Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n\n### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n- What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n- Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n- Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n\n### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n- What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n- Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n- [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n[Populated during initialization from memory_context() results, if any prior work exists]\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\nPopulate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n\n- Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n- Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n- Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n- Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n\nDo not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: [from config]\n- Convergence threshold: [from config]\n- Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n- Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n- Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n- Capability matrix: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n- Capability matrix doc: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n- Capability resolver: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n- Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n- Started: [timestamp]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":188,"totalLines":188,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1786568891638,"end":1786568891643}},"id":"prt_ff7cddac8001pLLB8nDsKoONEy","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7cdc000001pvCw5GzMAnw4Uc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786568892111,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_Z3WvMKtbD4ZRMKQX3tan6113","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Dashboard Template\n3: description: Template for the auto-generated dashboard file regenerated after every iteration from JSONL + strategy data. Provides human-readable session overview and recovery surface.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research dashboard\"\n6:   - \"research session overview\"\n7:   - \"research dashboard template\"\n8:   - \"research convergence trend\"\n9:   - \"research dead ends section\"\n10: importance_tier: normal\n11: contextType: general\n12: version: 1.14.0.9\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Research Dashboard - Session Overview\n16: \n17: Auto-generated from JSONL state log and strategy file. Regenerated after every iteration evaluation. Never manually edited.\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: ### Purpose\n22: \n23: Provides a compact, human-readable summary of the current research session. Serves three roles:\n24: 1. **Observability** — quick status check during long autonomous runs\n25: 2. **Recovery surface** — second recovery channel alongside JSONL after context compaction\n26: 3. **Lifecycle decision** — in confirm mode, shown before `resume` or `restart`\n27: \n28: ### Usage\n29: \n30: - **Location:** `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-dashboard.md`\n31: - **Generated by:** Orchestrator (step_generate_dashboard in YAML workflow)\n32: - **Data sources:** `deep-research-state.jsonl` + `findings-registry.json` + `deep-research-strategy.md`\n33: - **Protection:** `auto-generated` — overwritten each iteration, never manually edited\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## 2. STATUS\n38: - Topic: [from config]\n39: - Started: [from config.createdAt]\n40: - Status: [ITERATING | CONVERGING | STUCK_RECOVERY | COMPLETE]\n41: - Iteration: [N] of [maxIterations]\n42: - Session ID: [from config.lineage.sessionId]\n43: - Parent Session: [from config.lineage.parentSessionId or none]\n44: - Lifecycle Mode: [new | resume | restart]\n45: - Generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 3. PROGRESS\n50: \n51: | # | Focus | Track | Ratio | Findings | Status |\n52: |---|-------|-------|-------|----------|--------|\n53: | [per iteration from JSONL] |\n54: \n55: - iterationsCompleted: [from findings registry metrics]\n56: - keyFindings: [from findings registry metrics]\n57: - openQuestions: [from findings registry metrics]\n58: - resolvedQuestions: [from findings registry metrics]\n59: \n60: ---\n61: \n62: ## 4. QUESTIONS\n63: - Answered: [X/Y]\n64: - [x] Q1: [summary] (iteration N)\n65: - [ ] Q2: [remaining]\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: ## 5. TREND\n70: - Last 3 ratios: [0.XX -> 0.XX -> 0.XX] [improving | stable | declining]\n71: - Stuck count: [N]\n72: - Guard violations: [none | list]\n73: - convergenceScore: [from reducer metrics]\n74: - coverageBySources: [from reducer metrics]\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## 6. DEAD ENDS\n79: - [approach]: [reason] (iteration N)\n80: \n81: ---\n82: \n83: ## 6A. DIVERGENT PIVOTS\n84: - Completed pivots: [from findings registry]\n85: - Failed pivots: [from findings registry]\n86: - Audited overrides: [from findings registry]\n87: - Saturated directions: [from findings registry]\n88: - Remaining frontier: [from findings registry]\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: ## 7. NEXT FOCUS\n93: [from strategy.md \"Next Focus\" section]\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 8. ACTIVE RISKS\n98: - [guard violations, high stuck count, declining trend, etc.]\n99: - [migration events, reducer warnings, lifecycle conflicts]\n100: \n101: ---\n102: \n103: ## 9. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n104: \n105: Reference snippet showing what a rendered dashboard looks like after iteration 5 of a 10-iteration run. Use this as a visual anchor when inspecting a live dashboard.\n106: \n107: ```markdown\n108: # Deep Research Dashboard - Session Overview\n109: \n110: ## 2. STATUS\n111: - Topic: OpenCode plugin loader resilience\n112: - Started: 2026-04-20T09:14:22+02:00\n113: - Status: ITERATING\n114: - Iteration: 5 of 10\n115: - Session ID: dr-20260420-091422\n116: - Parent Session: none\n117: - Lifecycle Mode: new\n118: - Generation: 1\n119: \n120: ## 3. PROGRESS\n121: \n122: | # | Focus                       | Track        | Ratio | Findings | Status     |\n123: |---|-----------------------------|--------------|-------|----------|------------|\n124: | 1 | Entry-point discovery rules | architecture | 0.82  | 4        | converging |\n125: | 2 | ESM vs CommonJS interop     | runtime      | 0.64  | 3        | converging |\n126: | 3 | Plugin-load error surfaces  | observability| 0.47  | 2        | converging |\n127: | 4 | Host/plugin version gating  | lifecycle    | 0.35  | 2        | converging |\n128: | 5 | Cross-runtime parity        | portability  | 0.28  | 1        | converging |\n129: \n130: ## 5. CONVERGENCE TREND\n131: - Last 3 ratios: 0.47 -> 0.35 -> 0.28 (declining)\n132: - Stuck count: 0\n133: - Guard violations: none\n134: - convergenceScore: 0.71\n135: - coverageBySources: 0.83\n136: ```\n\n(End of file - total 136 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Dashboard Template\ndescription: Template for the auto-generated dashboard file regenerated after every iteration from JSONL + strategy data. Provides human-readable session overview and recovery surface.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep research dashboard\"\n  - \"research session overview\"\n  - \"research dashboard template\"\n  - \"research convergence trend\"\n  - \"research dead ends section\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.14.0.9\n---\n\n# Deep Research Dashboard - Session Overview\n\nAuto-generated from JSONL state log and strategy file. Regenerated after every iteration evaluation. Never manually edited.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Dashboard Template\ndescription: Template for the auto-generated dashboard file regenerated after every iteration from JSONL + strategy data. Provides human-readable session overview and recovery surface.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep research dashboard\"\n  - \"research session overview\"\n  - \"research dashboard template\"\n  - \"research convergence trend\"\n  - \"research dead ends section\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.14.0.9\n---\n\n# Deep Research Dashboard - Session Overview\n\nAuto-generated from JSONL state log and strategy file. Regenerated after every iteration evaluation. Never manually edited.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nProvides a compact, human-readable summary of the current research session. Serves three roles:\n1. **Observability** — quick status check during long autonomous runs\n2. **Recovery surface** — second recovery channel alongside JSONL after context compaction\n3. **Lifecycle decision** — in confirm mode, shown before `resume` or `restart`\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Location:** `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-dashboard.md`\n- **Generated by:** Orchestrator (step_generate_dashboard in YAML workflow)\n- **Data sources:** `deep-research-state.jsonl` + `findings-registry.json` + `deep-research-strategy.md`\n- **Protection:** `auto-generated` — overwritten each iteration, never manually edited\n\n---\n\n## 2. STATUS\n- Topic: [from config]\n- Started: [from config.createdAt]\n- Status: [ITERATING | CONVERGING | STUCK_RECOVERY | COMPLETE]\n- Iteration: [N] of [maxIterations]\n- Session ID: [from config.lineage.sessionId]\n- Parent Session: [from config.lineage.parentSessionId or none]\n- Lifecycle Mode: [new | resume | restart]\n- Generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n\n---\n\n## 3. PROGRESS\n\n| # | Focus | Track | Ratio | Findings | Status |\n|---|-------|-------|-------|----------|--------|\n| [per iteration from JSONL] |\n\n- iterationsCompleted: [from findings registry metrics]\n- keyFindings: [from findings registry metrics]\n- openQuestions: [from findings registry metrics]\n- resolvedQuestions: [from findings registry metrics]\n\n---\n\n## 4. QUESTIONS\n- Answered: [X/Y]\n- [x] Q1: [summary] (iteration N)\n- [ ] Q2: [remaining]\n\n---\n\n## 5. TREND\n- Last 3 ratios: [0.XX -> 0.XX -> 0.XX] [improving | stable | declining]\n- Stuck count: [N]\n- Guard violations: [none | list]\n- convergenceScore: [from reducer metrics]\n- coverageBySources: [from reducer metrics]\n\n---\n\n## 6. DEAD ENDS\n- [approach]: [reason] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 6A. DIVERGENT PIVOTS\n- Completed pivots: [from findings registry]\n- Failed pivots: [from findings registry]\n- Audited overrides: [from findings registry]\n- Saturated directions: [from findings registry]\n- Remaining frontier: [from findings registry]\n\n---\n\n## 7. NEXT FOCUS\n[from strategy.md \"Next Focus\" section]\n\n---\n\n## 8. ACTIVE RISKS\n- [guard violations, high stuck count, declining trend, etc.]\n- [migration events, reducer warnings, lifecycle conflicts]\n\n---\n\n## 9. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n\nReference snippet showing what a rendered dashboard looks like after iteration 5 of a 10-iteration run. Use this as a visual anchor when inspecting a live dashboard.\n\n```markdown\n# Deep Research Dashboard - Session Overview\n\n## 2. STATUS\n- Topic: OpenCode plugin loader resilience\n- Started: 2026-04-20T09:14:22+02:00\n- Status: ITERATING\n- Iteration: 5 of 10\n- Session ID: dr-20260420-091422\n- Parent Session: none\n- Lifecycle Mode: new\n- Generation: 1\n\n## 3. PROGRESS\n\n| # | Focus                       | Track        | Ratio | Findings | Status     |\n|---|-----------------------------|--------------|-------|----------|------------|\n| 1 | Entry-point discovery rules | architecture | 0.82  | 4        | converging |\n| 2 | ESM vs CommonJS interop     | runtime      | 0.64  | 3        | converging |\n| 3 | Plugin-load error surfaces  | observability| 0.47  | 2        | converging |\n| 4 | Host/plugin version gating  | lifecycle    | 0.35  | 2        | converging |\n| 5 | Cross-runtime parity        | portability  | 0.28  | 1        | converging |\n\n## 5. CONVERGENCE TREND\n- Last 3 ratios: 0.47 -> 0.35 -> 0.28 (declining)\n- Stuck count: 0\n- Guard violations: none\n- convergenceScore: 0.71\n- coverageBySources: 0.83\n```","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":136,"totalLines":136,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-dashboard.md","time":{"start":1786568892100,"end":1786568892109}},"id":"prt_ff7cddd01001B4gqDNFOWHf0xd","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7cdc000001pvCw5GzMAnw4Uc"}}
