{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569243852,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_ET_yDuoggAZwWH518v2lr1G1877","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output?\",\n    \"Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it?\"\n  ],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Why do rewrites underwhelm at the representation boundary?\",\n      \"answer\": \"The dialect tokenizes every protected range into an opaque ~48-char marker, the wire body is a two-message prompt, and the instruction asks the model to preserve facts/names/numbers/paths it can no longer see; the validator also accepts an unchanged echo via the restored.text === sourceText short-circuit.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:134-288\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/adapters.ts:96-100\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:183-222\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Which quality levers are wired versus gated fail-closed?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Temperature and thinking controls are gated fail-closed for the shipped DeepSeek preset (capabilities 'unknown'), so the reference-like profile returns exact-original before transport; the profile has no few-shot/token-rubric field; adjacent spans are not coalesced; no source-backed model quality tier exists.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:100-116\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/presets.ts:171-179\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/prompt.ts:21-32\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:37-46,265-288\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-broad-protection\",\n      \"title\": \"Protection covers structure, not just values\",\n      \"summary\": \"collectProtectedRanges protects fenced code, tables, headings, commands, list markers, links, URLs, paths, quoted literals, variables, flags, hashes, identifiers, and numbers; accepted ranges are only overlap-filtered, never merged.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:134-288\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-opaque-token\",\n      \"title\": \"Every span becomes a ~48-char opaque placeholder\",\n      \"summary\": \"createToken emits ⟦pcp:v1:{24-hex-namespace}:{index}:{12-hex-digest}⟧ with no readable semantics; the model must reproduce each exactly once in order.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:396-415\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-two-message-body\",\n      \"title\": \"Wire body is one system + one user message\",\n      \"summary\": \"messages() sends systemInstruction plus the whole encoded text; no token inventory, schema, or examples.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/adapters.ts:96-100\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-prompt-token-mismatch\",\n      \"title\": \"Prompt describes values the model cannot see\",\n      \"summary\": \"The instruction says 'keep every fact, name, number, and file path', but those values are already opaque ⟦pcp:v1:...⟧ tokens; the model is never told how to treat the placeholders.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/test/fixtures/prompt-profiles.json:13-56\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-echo-shortcircuit\",\n      \"title\": \"Unchanged echo is accepted without quality check\",\n      \"summary\": \"The Markdown-structure and semantic-veto stages run only inside if (restored.text !== sourceText), so a verbatim echo skips every readability/meaning check and is accepted.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:183-222\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-strict-restore\",\n      \"title\": \"Restoration is fail-closed on any token deviation\",\n      \"summary\": \"duplicate, changed, unexpected, missing, or reordered tokens all reject; token granularity therefore trades directly against model usability.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:133-181\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-control-gate\",\n      \"title\": \"DeepSeek temperature/thinking gated fail-closed\",\n      \"summary\": \"baseCapabilities(true) marks temperature/thinking 'unknown'; compilePromptControls requires state 'yes' + confidence 'confirmed', so the shipped preset + reference-like profile returns unsupported('temperature') and exact-original before transport.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/presets.ts:171-179\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:100-116\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/executor.ts:150-185\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-no-examples-field\",\n      \"title\": \"Prompt profile has no few-shot/rubric field\",\n      \"summary\": \"PromptProfileRecord has promptVersion, systemInstruction, copyEditingScope, protectedValuePolicyVersion, temperature, thinkingMode, providerControlMappings, unsupportedControlBehavior — no examples or token contract.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/prompt.ts:21-32\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-adjacent-inflation\",\n      \"title\": \"Adjacent spans are not coalesced\",\n      \"summary\": \"addRange only overlap-filters; each inline regex emits its own token, so a flag + number + path in one clause become three ~48-char tokens with no adjacent-span context.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:37-46,265-288\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-smoke-not-reproducible\",\n      \"title\": \"Live smoke is not reproducible through shipped preset\",\n      \"summary\": \"The smoke's modest rewrite implies fresh confirmed capability evidence (or a distinct profile) that is not checked into the package; the exact-original short-circuit otherwise fires first.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:71-76\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Relax token identity/order/count checks\",\n      \"reason\": \"Exact ordered restoration is the fail-closed privacy/fidelity boundary.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:133-181\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Treat the two-message wire body as a sufficient prompt\",\n      \"reason\": \"It carries no token contract or examples.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/adapters.ts:96-100\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Assume temperature alone fixes readability\",\n      \"reason\": \"Temperature cannot be applied through the shipped DeepSeek preset without fresh confirmed capability evidence.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:100-116\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Assume a model-tier upgrade is source-confirmed\",\n      \"reason\": \"No package source establishes a quality ranking across tiers.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/presets.ts:43-84\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n    \"openQuestions\": 2,\n    \"resolvedQuestions\": 2,\n    \"keyFindings\": 10,\n    \"convergenceScore\": 0,\n    \"coverageBySources\": { \"sourceFiles\": 10, \"sourceFamilies\": 6 }\n  },\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-deepseek-1786568849119-wn6hux\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"iterating\",\n  \"lastIteration\": 2,\n  \"nextFocus\": \"Iteration 3: trace whether the optional meaning-preservation judge is composed into the provider/runtime/render path and what plaintext it receives.\"\n}\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json","time":{"start":1786569243843,"end":1786569243850}},"id":"prt_ff7d2f9f5001r6JJGEbwMGCik3","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d2eb7a001qO0jqG5Hw8suP3"}}
