{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569468323,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_ET_uNsgDNjS9R0kLMf7hdYC1525","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [\n    \"Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it?\"\n  ],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Why do rewrites underwhelm at the representation boundary?\",\n      \"answer\": \"The dialect tokenizes every protected range into an opaque ~48-char marker, the wire body is a two-message prompt, and the instruction asks the model to preserve facts/names/numbers/paths it can no longer see; the validator also accepts an unchanged echo via the restored.text === sourceText short-circuit.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:134-288\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/adapters.ts:96-100\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:183-222\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Which quality levers are wired versus gated fail-closed?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Temperature and thinking controls are gated fail-closed for the shipped DeepSeek preset (capabilities 'unknown'), so the reference-like profile returns exact-original before transport; the profile has no few-shot/token-rubric field; adjacent spans are not coalesced; no source-backed model quality tier exists.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:100-116\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/presets.ts:171-179\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/prompt.ts:21-32\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:37-46,265-288\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is the meaning-preservation judge wired into the provider/runtime/render path?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No: executeProviderRoute returns a candidate and decideRender consumes a validation result, neither invoking the judge; evaluateFidelityVeto hard-disables it; the judge sees restored plaintext (a second egress if hosted); the offline proxy reviewer is provisional evidence, not a runtime validator.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/executor.ts:110-138\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:229-244,315-370\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/fidelity-veto.ts:30-50\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/proxy-judge.ts:32-58\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Is local-tokenize -> model -> restore the right architecture?\",\n      \"answer\": \"The primitive is the right security boundary but whole-message projection is the wrong granularity; the payload is raw text and the Codex adapter references canonical text IDs, so a hybrid deterministic skeleton plus bounded prose slots is the best fit; semantic diff is a safety gate, not a renderer; Codex is the only full-projection path.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/core/assembly-output.ts:66-99\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/runtimes/codex.ts:271-294,116-135\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/semantics.ts:61-107\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/clients/types.ts:101-105\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-broad-protection\",\n      \"title\": \"Protection covers structure, not just values\",\n      \"summary\": \"collectProtectedRanges protects fenced code, tables, headings, commands, list markers, links, URLs, paths, quoted literals, variables, flags, hashes, identifiers, and numbers; accepted ranges are only overlap-filtered, never merged.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:134-288\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-opaque-token\",\n      \"title\": \"Every span becomes a ~48-char opaque placeholder\",\n      \"summary\": \"createToken emits ⟦pcp:v1:{24-hex-namespace}:{index}:{12-hex-digest}⟧ with no readable semantics; the model must reproduce each exactly once in order.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:396-415\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-two-message-body\",\n      \"title\": \"Wire body is one system + one user message\",\n      \"summary\": \"messages() sends systemInstruction plus the whole encoded text; no token inventory, schema, or examples.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/adapters.ts:96-100\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-prompt-token-mismatch\",\n      \"title\": \"Prompt describes values the model cannot see\",\n      \"summary\": \"The instruction says 'keep every fact, name, number, and file path', but those values are already opaque ⟦pcp:v1:...⟧ tokens; the model is never told how to treat the placeholders.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/test/fixtures/prompt-profiles.json:13-56\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-echo-shortcircuit\",\n      \"title\": \"Unchanged echo is accepted without quality check\",\n      \"summary\": \"The Markdown-structure and semantic-veto stages run only inside if (restored.text !== sourceText), so a verbatim echo skips every readability/meaning check and is accepted.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:183-222\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1-strict-restore\",\n      \"title\": \"Restoration is fail-closed on any token deviation\",\n      \"summary\": \"duplicate, changed, unexpected, missing, or reordered tokens all reject; token granularity therefore trades directly against model usability.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:133-181\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-control-gate\",\n      \"title\": \"DeepSeek temperature/thinking gated fail-closed\",\n      \"summary\": \"baseCapabilities(true) marks temperature/thinking 'unknown'; compilePromptControls requires state 'yes' + confidence 'confirmed', so the shipped preset + reference-like profile returns unsupported('temperature') and exact-original before transport.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/presets.ts:171-179\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:100-116\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/executor.ts:150-185\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-no-examples-field\",\n      \"title\": \"Prompt profile has no few-shot/rubric field\",\n      \"summary\": \"PromptProfileRecord has promptVersion, systemInstruction, copyEditingScope, protectedValuePolicyVersion, temperature, thinkingMode, providerControlMappings, unsupportedControlBehavior — no examples or token contract.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/prompt.ts:21-32\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-adjacent-inflation\",\n      \"title\": \"Adjacent spans are not coalesced\",\n      \"summary\": \"addRange only overlap-filters; each inline regex emits its own token, so a flag + number + path in one clause become three ~48-char tokens with no adjacent-span context.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/dialect.ts:37-46,265-288\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f2-smoke-not-reproducible\",\n      \"title\": \"Live smoke is not reproducible through shipped preset\",\n      \"summary\": \"The smoke's modest rewrite implies fresh confirmed capability evidence (or a distinct profile) that is not checked into the package; the exact-original short-circuit otherwise fires first.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:71-76\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f3-no-runtime-judge\",\n      \"title\": \"Optional meaning judge is not composed into rendering\",\n      \"summary\": \"executeProviderRoute returns a candidate, decideRender consumes a validation result; no production source connects the candidate to validateProjectionCandidate with judgeMode required.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/executor.ts:110-138\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/render/decision.ts:40-91\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f3-veto-disables-judge\",\n      \"title\": \"Evaluation fidelity veto disables the judge\",\n      \"summary\": \"evaluateFidelityVeto calls validateProjectionCandidate with judgeMode 'disabled', so the deterministic evaluation lane never exercises the meaning judge.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/fidelity-veto.ts:30-50\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f3-judge-plaintext\",\n      \"title\": \"Judge seam receives restored plaintext values\",\n      \"summary\": \"runJudge passes sourceText (decoded) and restored.text (restored candidate), so a hosted judge would be a second egress of real protected values.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:175-181,317-357\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f3-semantics-restored\",\n      \"title\": \"Semantic veto operates on restored text\",\n      \"summary\": \"compareSemanticMeaning runs after restoration, so protected numbers/identifiers are already guaranteed; the veto can only catch prose-level drift, never awkwardness, verbosity, or a barely-changed rewrite.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/semantics.ts:61-107\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f3-proxy-provisional\",\n      \"title\": \"Offline proxy reviewer is provisional evidence\",\n      \"summary\": \"scoreMaskedReviewPacketWithProxy returns evidenceClass 'llm-proxy'; assertHumanCertifiable throws on proxy evidence, so it can rank profiles/models but never authorize a release.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/proxy-judge.ts:32-58\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/types.ts:28-38\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f4-raw-text-payload\",\n      \"title\": \"Projection payload is raw text, not typed fields\",\n      \"summary\": \"completeAssembly decodes the final assistant message's exact bytes to text; EventEnvelope.payload is an opaque JsonObject and the Codex adapter maps content to canonical references (textOriginalId, toolInputOriginalId, toolResultOriginalId).\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/core/assembly-output.ts:66-99\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/runtimes/codex.ts:271-294\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f4-deterministic-substrate\",\n      \"title\": \"Typed event envelope supports a deterministic shell\",\n      \"summary\": \"EventEnvelope carries typed kind, phase, terminalStatus, order coordinates, and canonical refs, so a deterministic renderer can format the shell of typed status/error/lifecycle messages without a model.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/event.ts:52-87\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/core/assembler.ts:122-260\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f4-hybrid-fit\",\n      \"title\": \"Hybrid skeleton + prose slots fits the boundaries\",\n      \"summary\": \"A deterministic skeleton for the structured shell plus bounded locally-protected prose slots for raw-text regions concentrates model work where it helps and reduces opaque-token burden; the primitive stays as the security boundary.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/core/assembly-output.ts:66-99\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/clients/types.ts:101-105\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f4-codex-only-full-projection\",\n      \"title\": \"Codex is the only full-projection path\",\n      \"summary\": \"CodexCapabilityRecords marks completeMessage and atomicRenderDecision CONFIRMED_YES but append and sidecar CONFIRMED_NO; full-projection parity requires ownsCompleteMessage && ownsAtomicRenderDecision.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"sources\": [\"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/runtimes/codex.ts:116-135\", \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/clients/types.ts:101-105\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Relax token identity/order/count checks\",\n      \"reason\": \"Exact ordered restoration is the fail-closed privacy/fidelity boundary.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:133-181\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Treat the two-message wire body as a sufficient prompt\",\n      \"reason\": \"It carries no token contract or examples.\",\n      \"iteration\": 1,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/adapters.ts:96-100\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Assume temperature alone fixes readability\",\n      \"reason\": \"Temperature cannot be applied through the shipped DeepSeek preset without fresh confirmed capability evidence.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/controls.ts:100-116\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Assume a model-tier upgrade is source-confirmed\",\n      \"reason\": \"No package source establishes a quality ranking across tiers.\",\n      \"iteration\": 2,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/providers/presets.ts:43-84\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Treat evaluateFidelityVeto as meaning-judge wiring\",\n      \"reason\": \"It hard-codes judgeMode 'disabled'.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/fidelity-veto.ts:30-50\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Use the masked LLM proxy reviewer as the runtime meaning gate\",\n      \"reason\": \"It is comparative provisional evidence, not a privacy-scoped reject-only validator.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/proxy-judge.ts:32-58\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Call a hosted judge after restoration\",\n      \"reason\": \"It would egress restored plaintext values as a second boundary.\",\n      \"iteration\": 3,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/validator.ts:175-181,317-357\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Replace local restoration with remote structured rendering\",\n      \"reason\": \"It moves exactness/privacy across the provider boundary without solving arbitrary assistant prose.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/protected-spans.ts:70-114\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Assume event kind alone supports universal templates\",\n      \"reason\": \"The projected body is raw text, not typed fields.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/runtimes/codex.ts:271-294\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"direction\": \"Use semantic diff as a readability generator\",\n      \"reason\": \"It is a deterministic rejection/diagnostic layer.\",\n      \"iteration\": 4,\n      \"source\": \"packages/cli-communication-projection/src/fidelity/semantics.ts:61-107\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"iterationsCompleted\": 4,\n    \"openQuestions\": 1,\n    \"resolvedQuestions\": 4,\n    \"keyFindings\": 19,\n    \"convergenceScore\": 0,\n    \"coverageBySources\": { \"sourceFiles\": 18, \"sourceFamilies\": 9 }\n  },\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-deepseek-1786568849119-wn6hux\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"iterating\",\n  \"lastIteration\": 4,\n  \"nextFocus\": \"Iteration 5: establish where projection earns its complexity versus deterministic formatting, grounded in the skill contract, evaluation evidence classes, privacy/rollback docs, and the release gate.\"\n}\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json","time":{"start":1786569468311,"end":1786569468321}},"id":"prt_ff7d62d66001BnpKeGTBWH68R1","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d61e3d001iceNz9O7VuI8jQ"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786569469037,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"id":"prt_ff7d6ac6a001phc0LAaaFbNSpH","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"3e93b46b8c8872cc83f51ee8902334db5ebb6d6a","messageID":"msg_ff7d61e3d001iceNz9O7VuI8jQ","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":186642,"input":892,"output":3990,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":181760}},"cost":0.0045182}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786569472424,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"id":"prt_ff7d6b9a7001V8yVp5unUJnWTT","messageID":"msg_ff7d6ae81001TS4XeV1UfRQ4zO","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","snapshot":"3e93b46b8c8872cc83f51ee8902334db5ebb6d6a","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569474501,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_BLTZV0sLNuPbxwHy1wKg1355","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Release runbook\n2: \n3: 1. Build and verify with `npm ci`, `npm run check`, and\n4:    `npx vitest run --config vitest.config.ts test/release`.\n5: 2. Run `npm pack --dry-run`; confirm only package metadata, `dist`, and `docs`\n6:    are present. Inspect the final tarball before distribution.\n7: 3. Install the exact tarball into a clean consumer and import every public\n8:    subpath using [install.md](./install.md).\n9: 4. Choose local-only, hosted, or mixed privacy explicitly. Confirm there is no\n10:    undeclared fallback.\n11: 5. Run the compatibility doctor with fresh runtime, protocol, provider, model,\n12:    privacy, and presentation evidence.\n13: 6. Run the deterministic six-runtime injected rehearsal and verify the\n14:    local-only transport spy records zero hosted calls.\n15: 7. Operator-run prerequisite: execute the real live credentialed provider smoke\n16:    in the approved environment. Supply credential references through the\n17:    approved secret store; never record values, prompts, responses, or raw\n18:    transcript content. This step is deliberately outside automated tests.\n19: 8. Operator-run prerequisite: complete the powered, blinded HUMAN\n20:    non-inferiority study. Proxy or synthetic scores are diagnostic only and do\n21:    not authorize release.\n22: 9. Assemble fresh provider, runtime, fidelity, privacy, evaluation, doctor, and\n23:    strict-validation evidence. Release only when the fail-closed gate returns\n24:    `release-ready`.\n25: 10. Retain the previous exact tarball and rehearse [rollback.md](./rollback.md)\n26:     before rollout.\n27: \n28: Stop and select original-only mode on any missing, stale, provisional,\n29: contradictory, or failed release prerequisite.\n\n(End of file - total 29 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Release runbook\n\n1. Build and verify with `npm ci`, `npm run check`, and\n   `npx vitest run --config vitest.config.ts test/release`.\n2. Run `npm pack --dry-run`; confirm only package metadata, `dist`, and `docs`\n   are present. Inspect the final tarball before distribution.\n3. Install the exact tarball into a clean consumer and import every public\n   subpath using [install.md](./install.md).\n4. Choose local-only, hosted, or mixed privacy explicitly. Confirm there is no\n   undeclared fallback.\n5. Run the compatibility doctor with fresh runtime, protocol, provider, model,\n   privacy, and presentation evidence.\n6. Run the deterministic six-runtime injected rehearsal and verify the\n   local-only transport spy records zero hosted calls.\n7. Operator-run prerequisite: execute the real live credentialed provider smoke\n   in the approved environment. Supply credential references through the\n   approved secret store; never record values, prompts, responses, or raw\n   transcript content. This step is deliberately outside automated tests.\n8. Operator-run prerequisite: complete the powered, blinded HUMAN\n   non-inferiority study. Proxy or synthetic scores are diagnostic only and do","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md","text":"# Release runbook\n\n1. Build and verify with `npm ci`, `npm run check`, and\n   `npx vitest run --config vitest.config.ts test/release`.\n2. Run `npm pack --dry-run`; confirm only package metadata, `dist`, and `docs`\n   are present. Inspect the final tarball before distribution.\n3. Install the exact tarball into a clean consumer and import every public\n   subpath using [install.md](./install.md).\n4. Choose local-only, hosted, or mixed privacy explicitly. Confirm there is no\n   undeclared fallback.\n5. Run the compatibility doctor with fresh runtime, protocol, provider, model,\n   privacy, and presentation evidence.\n6. Run the deterministic six-runtime injected rehearsal and verify the\n   local-only transport spy records zero hosted calls.\n7. Operator-run prerequisite: execute the real live credentialed provider smoke\n   in the approved environment. Supply credential references through the\n   approved secret store; never record values, prompts, responses, or raw\n   transcript content. This step is deliberately outside automated tests.\n8. Operator-run prerequisite: complete the powered, blinded HUMAN\n   non-inferiority study. Proxy or synthetic scores are diagnostic only and do\n   not authorize release.\n9. Assemble fresh provider, runtime, fidelity, privacy, evaluation, doctor, and\n   strict-validation evidence. Release only when the fail-closed gate returns\n   `release-ready`.\n10. Retain the previous exact tarball and rehearse [rollback.md](./rollback.md)\n    before rollout.\n\nStop and select original-only mode on any missing, stale, provisional,\ncontradictory, or failed release prerequisite.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":29,"totalLines":29,"truncated":false}},"title":"packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md","time":{"start":1786569474494,"end":1786569474499}},"id":"prt_ff7d6bfb0001q94F32G8Yn2g9K","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d6ae81001TS4XeV1UfRQ4zO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569475073,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_hxG9BnytO4QWTPnm2XTt3765","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/rollback.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/rollback.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Rollback\n2: \n3: Keep the previous exact tarball in a local release cache. Rollback does not\n4: require a provider call and must not modify the canonical transcript.\n5: \n6: 1. Disable new projections.\n7: 2. Select `OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode` from the `release` entry point.\n8: 3. Install the previous exact local tarball.\n9: 4. Verify the canonical transcript digest is unchanged.\n10: 5. Run the compatibility doctor before re-enabling any projection route.\n11: \n12: ```sh\n13: export PREVIOUS_PACKAGE_TARBALL=/srv/releases/portable-cli-communication-projection-0.0.9.tgz\n14: npm install --offline --save-exact \"$PREVIOUS_PACKAGE_TARBALL\"\n15: node ./operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs\n16: ```\n17: \n18: ```js\n19: import {\n20:   OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode,\n21:   planRollback,\n22: } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/release';\n23: \n24: const plan = planRollback({\n25:   previousPackageVersion: '0.0.9',\n26:   canonicalTranscriptDigest: process.env.CANONICAL_TRANSCRIPT_DIGEST,\n27:   trigger: 'operator-request',\n28: });\n29: \n30: if (OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode.networkRequired || plan.mutatesCanonicalTranscript) {\n31:   throw new Error('Unsafe rollback plan.');\n32: }\n33: console.log(JSON.stringify(plan));\n34: ```\n35: \n36: The digest is integrity metadata, not transcript content. Do not place raw\n37: transcript bytes or credential values in rollback logs.\n\n(End of file - total 37 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Rollback\n\nKeep the previous exact tarball in a local release cache. Rollback does not\nrequire a provider call and must not modify the canonical transcript.\n\n1. Disable new projections.\n2. Select `OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode` from the `release` entry point.\n3. Install the previous exact local tarball.\n4. Verify the canonical transcript digest is unchanged.\n5. Run the compatibility doctor before re-enabling any projection route.\n\n```sh\nexport PREVIOUS_PACKAGE_TARBALL=/srv/releases/portable-cli-communication-projection-0.0.9.tgz\nnpm install --offline --save-exact \"$PREVIOUS_PACKAGE_TARBALL\"\nnode ./operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs\n```\n\n```js\nimport {\n  OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/rollback.md","text":"# Rollback\n\nKeep the previous exact tarball in a local release cache. Rollback does not\nrequire a provider call and must not modify the canonical transcript.\n\n1. Disable new projections.\n2. Select `OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode` from the `release` entry point.\n3. Install the previous exact local tarball.\n4. Verify the canonical transcript digest is unchanged.\n5. Run the compatibility doctor before re-enabling any projection route.\n\n```sh\nexport PREVIOUS_PACKAGE_TARBALL=/srv/releases/portable-cli-communication-projection-0.0.9.tgz\nnpm install --offline --save-exact \"$PREVIOUS_PACKAGE_TARBALL\"\nnode ./operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs\n```\n\n```js\nimport {\n  OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode,\n  planRollback,\n} from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/release';\n\nconst plan = planRollback({\n  previousPackageVersion: '0.0.9',\n  canonicalTranscriptDigest: process.env.CANONICAL_TRANSCRIPT_DIGEST,\n  trigger: 'operator-request',\n});\n\nif (OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode.networkRequired || plan.mutatesCanonicalTranscript) {\n  throw new Error('Unsafe rollback plan.');\n}\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(plan));\n```\n\nThe digest is integrity metadata, not transcript content. Do not place raw\ntranscript bytes or credential values in rollback logs.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":37,"totalLines":37,"truncated":false}},"title":"packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/rollback.md","time":{"start":1786569475068,"end":1786569475072}},"id":"prt_ff7d6c214001AC9VAlkU5Kbsfu","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d6ae81001TS4XeV1UfRQ4zO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569475640,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_Iu9wfOFDoiG1MsS3gtuc1869","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/support-matrix.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/support-matrix.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Support matrix\n2: \n3: Import `SupportMatrix` and `assessSupportMatrixFreshness` from\n4: `@portable-cli/communication-projection/release`. The matrix publishes dated,\n5: content-free claims for runtime, protocol, provider, model, operating system,\n6: prompt profile, and presentation tier.\n7: \n8: ```js\n9: import {\n10:   SupportMatrix,\n11:   assessSupportMatrixFreshness,\n12: } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/release';\n13: \n14: const result = assessSupportMatrixFreshness(SupportMatrix, new Date().toISOString());\n15: console.log(JSON.stringify({ status: result.status, reasons: result.reasonCodes }));\n16: if (result.decision !== 'allow') process.exitCode = 1;\n17: ```\n18: \n19: `supported` means the dated evidence supports release use. `provisional` needs\n20: operator confirmation. `unsupported`, malformed dates, and expired evidence\n21: block the route. A compatible major version is not enough when its evidence is\n22: stale.\n23: \n24: The automated six-runtime rehearsal uses injected transports and synthetic,\n25: content-free fixtures. A real credentialed provider smoke is an operator-run\n26: release prerequisite and must never be replaced by the injected rehearsal.\n\n(End of file - total 26 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Support matrix\n\nImport `SupportMatrix` and `assessSupportMatrixFreshness` from\n`@portable-cli/communication-projection/release`. The matrix publishes dated,\ncontent-free claims for runtime, protocol, provider, model, operating system,\nprompt profile, and presentation tier.\n\n```js\nimport {\n  SupportMatrix,\n  assessSupportMatrixFreshness,\n} from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/release';\n\nconst result = assessSupportMatrixFreshness(SupportMatrix, new Date().toISOString());\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ status: result.status, reasons: result.reasonCodes }));\nif (result.decision !== 'allow') process.exitCode = 1;\n```\n\n`supported` means the dated evidence supports release use. `provisional` needs\noperator confirmation. `unsupported`, malformed dates, and expired evidence","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/support-matrix.md","text":"# Support matrix\n\nImport `SupportMatrix` and `assessSupportMatrixFreshness` from\n`@portable-cli/communication-projection/release`. The matrix publishes dated,\ncontent-free claims for runtime, protocol, provider, model, operating system,\nprompt profile, and presentation tier.\n\n```js\nimport {\n  SupportMatrix,\n  assessSupportMatrixFreshness,\n} from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/release';\n\nconst result = assessSupportMatrixFreshness(SupportMatrix, new Date().toISOString());\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ status: result.status, reasons: result.reasonCodes }));\nif (result.decision !== 'allow') process.exitCode = 1;\n```\n\n`supported` means the dated evidence supports release use. `provisional` needs\noperator confirmation. `unsupported`, malformed dates, and expired evidence\nblock the route. A compatible major version is not enough when its evidence is\nstale.\n\nThe automated six-runtime rehearsal uses injected transports and synthetic,\ncontent-free fixtures. A real credentialed provider smoke is an operator-run\nrelease prerequisite and must never be replaced by the injected rehearsal.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":26,"totalLines":26,"truncated":false}},"title":"packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/support-matrix.md","time":{"start":1786569475634,"end":1786569475639}},"id":"prt_ff7d6c4510010Cu1uyZvpwZChG","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d6ae81001TS4XeV1UfRQ4zO"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569476212,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_8X6STKmLPZxDfJoPnJQd4280","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/configuration.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/configuration.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Configuration\n2: \n3: Choose one privacy mode explicitly. An ineligible or failed route returns the\n4: exact original; it never selects an undeclared provider.\n5: \n6: | Mode | Candidate providers | Egress consent | Fallback |\n7: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n8: | Local-only | Local endpoints only | `false` | `none` |\n9: | Hosted | Named hosted endpoints only | `true` | `none`, unless an explicit list is approved |\n10: | Mixed | Named local and hosted endpoints | `true` | Explicit ordered list only |\n11: \n12: Local-only policies should allow only `local-offline` and, when required,\n13: `local-networked`. Hosted policies must require fresh retention and training-use\n14: facts. Mixed policies must name every cross-class fallback and set\n15: `preservePrivacyClass` deliberately; ranking never creates a fallback.\n16: \n17: ## Compatibility doctor\n18: \n19: Save the following as `operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs`. It is\n20: a deterministic local configuration check: the injected reachability result\n21: contains no payload or credential. For a release, replace that injected result\n22: with the operator's bounded endpoint probe while keeping the same request and\n23: result types.\n24: \n25: ```js\n26: import { runCompatibilityDoctor } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/doctor';\n27: import { createOllamaModelRecord } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/providers';\n28: import { RuntimeCapabilityMatrix } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/runtimes';\n29: \n30: const now = '2026-08-12T12:00:00.000Z';\n31: const runtime = RuntimeCapabilityMatrix[0];\n32: if (!runtime) throw new Error('No supported runtime path is published.');\n33: \n34: const provider = createOllamaModelRecord({\n35:   modelId: 'operator-selected-model',\n36:   privacyClass: 'local-offline',\n37:   observedAt: '2026-08-12T00:00:00.000Z',\n38:   capabilitiesExpireAt: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z',\n39: });\n40: \n41: const report = await runCompatibilityDoctor({\n42:   proposedRuntimes: [{\n43:     runtime: runtime.runtime,\n44:     pathId: runtime.pathId,\n45:     runtimeVersion: runtime.testedVersions.runtime,\n46:     protocol: runtime.protocol,\n47:     protocolVersion: runtime.testedVersions.protocol,\n48:     presentationTier: runtime.presentationTier,\n49:   }],\n50:   proposedProviders: [provider],\n51:   proposedModels: [{\n52:     providerId: provider.provider.providerId,\n53:     modelId: provider.provider.modelId,\n54:     requiredCapabilities: [],\n55:   }],\n56:   credentialReferencePresence: [],\n57:   reachabilityProbe: async () => ({ status: 'reachable', durationMs: 0 }),\n58:   perProbeDeadlineMs: 1_000,\n59:   totalDeadlineMs: 2_000,\n60:   now,\n61: });\n62: \n63: console.log(JSON.stringify(report));\n64: if (report.overallDecision === 'blocked') process.exitCode = 1;\n65: ```\n66: \n67: Run it with `node ./operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs`. Treat a\n68: blocked report as original-only and a degraded report as requiring explicit\n69: operator review. Refresh dated evidence instead of bypassing a stale finding.\n\n(End of file - total 69 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Configuration\n\nChoose one privacy mode explicitly. An ineligible or failed route returns the\nexact original; it never selects an undeclared provider.\n\n| Mode | Candidate providers | Egress consent | Fallback |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Local-only | Local endpoints only | `false` | `none` |\n| Hosted | Named hosted endpoints only | `true` | `none`, unless an explicit list is approved |\n| Mixed | Named local and hosted endpoints | `true` | Explicit ordered list only |\n\nLocal-only policies should allow only `local-offline` and, when required,\n`local-networked`. Hosted policies must require fresh retention and training-use\nfacts. Mixed policies must name every cross-class fallback and set\n`preservePrivacyClass` deliberately; ranking never creates a fallback.\n\n## Compatibility doctor\n\nSave the following as `operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs`. It is\na deterministic local configuration check: the injected reachability result","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/configuration.md","text":"# Configuration\n\nChoose one privacy mode explicitly. An ineligible or failed route returns the\nexact original; it never selects an undeclared provider.\n\n| Mode | Candidate providers | Egress consent | Fallback |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Local-only | Local endpoints only | `false` | `none` |\n| Hosted | Named hosted endpoints only | `true` | `none`, unless an explicit list is approved |\n| Mixed | Named local and hosted endpoints | `true` | Explicit ordered list only |\n\nLocal-only policies should allow only `local-offline` and, when required,\n`local-networked`. Hosted policies must require fresh retention and training-use\nfacts. Mixed policies must name every cross-class fallback and set\n`preservePrivacyClass` deliberately; ranking never creates a fallback.\n\n## Compatibility doctor\n\nSave the following as `operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs`. It is\na deterministic local configuration check: the injected reachability result\ncontains no payload or credential. For a release, replace that injected result\nwith the operator's bounded endpoint probe while keeping the same request and\nresult types.\n\n```js\nimport { runCompatibilityDoctor } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/doctor';\nimport { createOllamaModelRecord } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/providers';\nimport { RuntimeCapabilityMatrix } from '@portable-cli/communication-projection/runtimes';\n\nconst now = '2026-08-12T12:00:00.000Z';\nconst runtime = RuntimeCapabilityMatrix[0];\nif (!runtime) throw new Error('No supported runtime path is published.');\n\nconst provider = createOllamaModelRecord({\n  modelId: 'operator-selected-model',\n  privacyClass: 'local-offline',\n  observedAt: '2026-08-12T00:00:00.000Z',\n  capabilitiesExpireAt: '2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z',\n});\n\nconst report = await runCompatibilityDoctor({\n  proposedRuntimes: [{\n    runtime: runtime.runtime,\n    pathId: runtime.pathId,\n    runtimeVersion: runtime.testedVersions.runtime,\n    protocol: runtime.protocol,\n    protocolVersion: runtime.testedVersions.protocol,\n    presentationTier: runtime.presentationTier,\n  }],\n  proposedProviders: [provider],\n  proposedModels: [{\n    providerId: provider.provider.providerId,\n    modelId: provider.provider.modelId,\n    requiredCapabilities: [],\n  }],\n  credentialReferencePresence: [],\n  reachabilityProbe: async () => ({ status: 'reachable', durationMs: 0 }),\n  perProbeDeadlineMs: 1_000,\n  totalDeadlineMs: 2_000,\n  now,\n});\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(report));\nif (report.overallDecision === 'blocked') process.exitCode = 1;\n```\n\nRun it with `node ./operator/run-communication-projection-doctor.mjs`. Treat a\nblocked report as original-only and a degraded report as requiring explicit\noperator review. Refresh dated evidence instead of bypassing a stale finding.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":69,"totalLines":69,"truncated":false}},"title":"packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/configuration.md","time":{"start":1786569476203,"end":1786569476210}},"id":"prt_ff7d6c68d001n2AReNaS5HDy5H","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d6ae81001TS4XeV1UfRQ4zO"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786569476740,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"id":"prt_ff7d6ca81001rwZ60aWrAm1xP6","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"3e93b46b8c8872cc83f51ee8902334db5ebb6d6a","messageID":"msg_ff7d6ae81001TS4XeV1UfRQ4zO","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":187043,"input":34,"output":318,"reasoning":67,"cache":{"write":0,"read":186624}},"cost":0.001026252}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786569479521,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"id":"prt_ff7d6d5600010rqQ2DlO5Hi5oL","messageID":"msg_ff7d6cc15001s7BHxyMfJ8iggz","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","snapshot":"3e93b46b8c8872cc83f51ee8902334db5ebb6d6a","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569506254,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_6xRgGMe4QfCPDXYekYCP3653","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: Value — where projection earns its complexity\n\n## Focus\n\nEstablish whether the capability earns its complexity and which use cases justify a model round-trip versus simpler deterministic formatting. Angle: VALUE, grounded in the skill contract, privacy/configuration/runbook/support-matrix/rollback docs, and the evaluation evidence classes.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the skill's WHEN TO USE / WHEN NOT TO USE and ALWAYS/NEVER rules.\n- Read the privacy, configuration, runbook, support-matrix, and rollback docs.\n- Read the evaluation evidence-class contract and the release-gate prerequisites.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The capability is explicitly scoped away from durable content. The skill's WHEN NOT TO USE excludes \"rewriting durable Markdown or any on-disk file\" — that \"changes canonical bytes and is explicitly out of scope\". So the value claim is bounded to transient display of a terminal message, not authored artifacts. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-communication/SKILL.md:33-40]\n\n2. The complexity ledger is real and gate-heavy. A live path requires: protected-span representation, privacy classification before ranking, provider routing, prompt profiles, capability-freshness checks, restoration, deterministic semantic vetoes, an optional judge, runtime/client ownership, content-free telemetry, a compatibility doctor, a six-runtime injected rehearsal, a real credentialed provider smoke, and a powered blinded human non-inferiority study. Every one of these is a prerequisite or an invariant, not optional polish. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-communication/SKILL.md:143-160] [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md:3-29]\n\n3. Release is gated on human evidence, not proxy scores. The runbook's step 8 requires \"the powered, blinded HUMAN non-inferiority study\"; proxy or synthetic scores are \"diagnostic only and do not authorize release\". `assertHumanCertifiable` throws on any `llm-proxy` or provisional result. This means the value question cannot be settled by another model's opinion — it requires measured human comprehension benefit. [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md:19-21] [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/types.ts:28-38]\n\n4. The high-value slice is complex, multi-sentence, user-facing prose. The two presentation tiers (`full-projection` vs `safe-native`) and `canClaimFullProjectionParity` (requires `ownsCompleteMessage && ownsAtomicRenderDecision`) imply full projection is only for a complete, atomically-owned message. Short statuses, typed lifecycle events, command/result summaries, raw tool data, secret-heavy diagnostics, and incomplete streams have little incremental readability value from a model and carry added latency/failure modes. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-communication/SKILL.md:132-135] [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/src/clients/types.ts:101-105] [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/event.ts:52-87]\n\n5. Privacy and consent further narrow the admissible value boundary. Hosted routing requires a named provider/model, operator consent, and fresh retention/training facts; local-only forbids hosted identifiers; mixed requires an explicit ordered fallback list. Any missing/stale/contradictory fact fails closed to the exact original. So value is only claimable inside an explicitly approved privacy mode — never a silent quality upgrade. [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/privacy.md:7-32] [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/configuration.md:1-15]\n\n6. The rollback contract makes a low-risk experiment feasible. Rollback disables projections, selects `OriginalOnlyEmergencyMode`, reinstalls the previous exact tarball offline, and verifies the canonical transcript digest — no provider call, no canonical mutation. This means a narrow deterministic-first rollout with append/sidecar (safe-native) is reversible by construction, which is the correct first value test. [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/rollback.md:1-37]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Enabling projection for every message: short/structured output has little incremental value while every model route adds latency, provider, validation, and fallback cost.\n- Using hosted routing as a default quality upgrade: it requires consent and fresh privacy evidence, with no source-backed provider/tier winner.\n- Treating proxy/synthetic/injected evidence as product-value proof: release requires human-certified non-inferiority.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- No user-value benchmark or deterministic prose baseline exists in the package; the value claim is therefore a contract-grounded hypothesis, not a measured ROI.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The supplied DeepSeek smoke is an anecdote, not a benchmark statistic; iterations 1-2 established its reproducibility gap.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-communication/SKILL.md:33-40,117-160]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/privacy.md:1-32]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/configuration.md:1-15]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/runbook.md:3-29]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/support-matrix.md:19-26]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/docs/rollback.md:1-37]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/src/evaluation/types.ts:28-38]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/src/clients/types.ts:101-105]\n- [SOURCE: packages/cli-communication-projection/src/contracts/event.ts:52-87]\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.70\n- Novelty justification: converting the privacy/consent, human-evidence, and rollback contracts into a concrete reversible deterministic-first adoption boundary is a new value framing versus a generic \"projection is nice to have\".\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked: reading the runbook, privacy, configuration, support-matrix, and rollback docs as a set turned value into a gated, reversible decision boundary rather than a vague judgment.\n- What did not work: no in-package user-value metric exists, so the value conclusion must remain conditional and explicitly unmeasured.\n- What I would do differently: the next concrete step is a fixed-corpus comparison of deterministic skeleton, whole-message projection, and hybrid slot projection on multi-sentence warnings/recovery messages.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nPhase synthesis: reconcile all five iterations into `research.md` and `resource-map.md`, preserving the open quality-efficacy question and the conditional deterministic-first value recommendation.\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","time":{"start":1786569506249,"end":1786569506253}},"id":"prt_ff7d6efaf001swAR7UTqXEt4Z4","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7d6cc15001s7BHxyMfJ8iggz"}}
