{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786569713246,"sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_00_DQewuSz5t8ieKCAWJjL87357","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","newString":"## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [x] Why do rewrites underwhelm, and which tokenization, prompt, profile, model-tier, and judge changes improve readability without weakening privacy or exact fidelity? (iterations 1-3)\n- [x] Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output? (iteration 4)\n- [x] Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it? (iteration 5)\n- [ ] Quality efficacy versus the deterministic baseline still requires a fixed-corpus comparison and human evidence. (open)","oldString":"## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Why do rewrites underwhelm, and which tokenization, prompt, profile, model-tier, and judge changes improve readability without weakening privacy or exact fidelity?\n- [ ] Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output?\n- [ ] Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it?"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -16,11 +16,12 @@\n Deep-research the communication-projection capability and the sk-communication skill. The pipeline tokenizes protected spans locally, sends only tokenized prose to a model, restores real values locally, and fails closed to the exact original when fidelity breaks. A live DeepSeek smoke produced only modestly improved rewrites: some barely changed, one with prose artifacts. Root cause is attributed to aggressive tokenization (many opaque tokens the model must carry verbatim) and a meaning-preservation judge not wired into the path. This lineage must verify and refine that attribution from the real source.\n \n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n \n-- [ ] Why do rewrites underwhelm, and which tokenization, prompt, profile, model-tier, and judge changes improve readability without weakening privacy or exact fidelity?\n-- [ ] Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output?\n-- [ ] Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it?\n+- [x] Why do rewrites underwhelm, and which tokenization, prompt, profile, model-tier, and judge changes improve readability without weakening privacy or exact fidelity? (iterations 1-3)\n+- [x] Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output? (iteration 4)\n+- [x] Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it? (iteration 5)\n+- [ ] Quality efficacy versus the deterministic baseline still requires a fixed-corpus comparison and human evidence. (open)\n \n ## 4. NON-GOALS\n \n - Implementing changes in the package or skill.\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0143-skilled-provider-adapters-privacy/specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -16,11 +16,12 @@\n Deep-research the communication-projection capability and the sk-communication skill. The pipeline tokenizes protected spans locally, sends only tokenized prose to a model, restores real values locally, and fails closed to the exact original when fidelity breaks. A live DeepSeek smoke produced only modestly improved rewrites: some barely changed, one with prose artifacts. Root cause is attributed to aggressive tokenization (many opaque tokens the model must carry verbatim) and a meaning-preservation judge not wired into the path. This lineage must verify and refine that attribution from the real source.\n \n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n \n-- [ ] Why do rewrites underwhelm, and which tokenization, prompt, profile, model-tier, and judge changes improve readability without weakening privacy or exact fidelity?\n-- [ ] Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output?\n-- [ ] Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it?\n+- [x] Why do rewrites underwhelm, and which tokenization, prompt, profile, model-tier, and judge changes improve readability without weakening privacy or exact fidelity? (iterations 1-3)\n+- [x] Is local-tokenize -> model -> local-restore the right architecture, or would structured/templated rendering, semantic diffing, or a hybrid produce better readable and safe output? (iteration 4)\n+- [x] Does projection earn its complexity over deterministic formatting, and which use cases justify it? (iteration 5)\n+- [ ] Quality efficacy versus the deterministic baseline still requires a fixed-corpus comparison and human evidence. (open)\n \n ## 4. NON-GOALS\n \n - Implementing changes in the package or skill.\n","additions":4,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"specs/sk-doc/028-sk-communication-skill/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1786569713243,"end":1786569713245}},"id":"prt_ff7da4f8a0010b1PGRC1DdH6jO","sessionID":"ses_00832c111ffe8md0OBtHNejm4h","messageID":"msg_ff7da3441001JUAiG1Zbizt8Cd"}}
